Z||000000||Jncomutt||11-18-2001||01:11 AM||||I know I should have went out and actually looked at the car before posting but its getting late and I'm lazy right now.<P>From reading some back posts/archives, what I understand is that my 84 duke has 2 belts, and one of the 2 is just to run the AC compressor.  Well Since my ac compressor doesn't work, Can I take the belt off of it?  I think it squeeks and i'm not going to use AC over the winter anyways.<P>So does this belt drive something else too?  OR can I just take it off??||||reg||1
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||11-18-2001||01:17 AM||||You should have 1 belt that runs the alt. and the water pump, and 1 for the a/c.  I have the a/c out of my '84 SE, and just the one belt.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brandon86SE||11-18-2001||01:32 AM||||Yup, I've been running w/out an AC belt for a little over a month now.  I have a new belt and everything, just that it's a real pain to get on.  Me and my friend fought with it for a few hours the day we removed the old squeaking one.  I decided it's something I can put off since I won't need ac for a while now.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||SLYGUY||11-18-2001||03:28 AM||||While it makes sense to not need the A/C in some of the cold climates that you guys are in you might still need it. The defroster uses the dehumidifier which is an integral part of the A/C system. Without that it will take much longer to defrost your windshield if it will in fact defrost at all. <P>Here in CA air conditioning is a must have and when it gets bone chilling in the winter (read: under 60F) a defroster can be a lifesaver. <P>Just my $.02<P>Sly<P>||||reg||1
